A||||3||btoth||Computer dilemma||||5||
Z||000000||btoth||12-02-2001||01:14 PM||||The dilemma:<P>My CD writer can't read the CDs that it writes.  My 33x CD-ROM bit the dust, so I'm using an old 4x... which can't read the CDs that I make, either.  My Dads old 4x can't read the CDs, but his new laptop CD-ROM drive can, and so can all of my friends new CD-ROM/DVD-ROM drives.  So, that would lead me to believe that the old CD-ROMs can't read CDRs... but no... both my 4x and my CD writer can read CDRs made by my friends CD writer, and they can read any CDRs that I made previous to this spring.  Which would lead me to believe that maybe it's the new cheap CDR media that the stores are selling.  But that wouldn't explain why the CDs I write can be read in other peoples drives!  So, it's not the media, and it's not the write head in my CD writer because obviously, the CDs do work.  And both drives can read old media (by old, I'm talking about CDRs made for 4x or 8x burners) and original CDs... so they can read just fine (except for the stuff I've been trying to copy the last 6 months).<P>So is it just that an older 4x CD-ROM and a 4x4x16 CD burner don't read the new 16x media well???  I'm stumped.  Does this even make sense??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||12-02-2001||01:24 PM||||If the writer can't read the CDR that it writes itself, then there's something wrong with the writer...||||reg||1
Z||000002||8Ball||12-02-2001||05:50 PM||||Well as for the older cd readers not being able to read the burned cd's, You are burnign them at too high a speed. Try burning on 1 or 2 speed for the older cdrom's. Now as for the burner not being able to read them, Is it an off brand burner? If so it may be the same problem. Cannot read the cd's burned at higher speed. Or the laser may be misaligned. In which case you need a new burner.<P>E.B.<BR>Senior Tech for A.S.I.||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||12-03-2001||12:30 PM||||Actually, it was a pretty good Yamaha.  I guess I just used it too much.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Got the newest Yamaha drive yesterday.  Really cool.  And it can read and write all the sublayer info that my older one couldn't.  Plus its a 24x writer, but it slows down to the speed of the media that it's writing too.  And the 8MB buffer is nice too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm excited.  Early Christmas present.||||reg||1
